    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0133" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg59"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 28, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the note which you did me
                    the honor to address to me on the 15th December last, relative to shot fired
                    from a battery at Eastport, having fallen on British territory, I am directed by
                    her Majesty’s government to state to you that they have received with
                    satisfaction the assurance contained in your above-mentioned note, that
                    instructions will be given to prevent any further shots being fired from the
                    battery at Eastport into British territory, and that the occurrence in question
                    was unauthorized, inadvertent, and was to be regretted.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
